---
import EditorialFrame from '../../components/EditorialFrame.astro';
import SourceAvailabilityNotice from '../../components/SourceAvailabilityNotice.astro';
import { records, services, fmtDate } from '../../lib/data.js';
import { newestDate } from '../../lib/editorial.js';

const rows = records.filter(record => record.jurisdiction === 'NO' && record.status === 'ok')
  .sort((a, b) => b.value_days - a.value_days || a.service_name.localeCompare(b.service_name));
const changes = rows.filter(record => record.delta && record.delta.dir !== 'flat');
const checked = rows.map(record => record.effective_date).sort().at(-1);
const sources = [...new Set(rows.map(record => record.source_url))];
const maxDays = Math.max(...rows.map(record => record.value_days), 1);
const source = rows[0]?.sourceMeta;
---
<EditorialFrame
  sectionName="Reports"
  sectionPath="/reports/"
  slug="norway-processing-time-changes"
  title={`Norway UDI last-verified waiting-time baseline — ${fmtDate(checked)}`}
  description={`Preserved UDI waiting-time baseline across ${rows.length} table-backed Norway immigration routes, with source dates, last verification and explicit source-access status.`}
  h1="Norway UDI last-verified waiting-time baseline"
  lede={`This report preserves ${rows.length} table-backed UDI waiting-time routes across ${sources.length} source pages. Automated access is currently unavailable, so these figures are a last-verified baseline—not a claim about UDI’s current values.`}
  published="2026-08-30"
  modified={newestDate('2026-09-24', checked)}
  checked={checked}
  about={['Norway immigration waiting times', 'UDI processing times', 'waiting-time history']}
  citations={sources}
  adPrefix="report-no"
>
  <div class="stats">
    <div><div class="n">{rows.length}</div><div class="l">routes preserved</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">{sources.length}</div><div class="l">official table pages</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">{fmtDate(checked)}</div><div class="l">latest source update</div></div>
    <div><div class="n">{changes.length}</div><div class="l">verified changes</div></div>
  </div>
  <SourceAvailabilityNotice source={source} />

  {changes.length === 0 ? (
    <div class="callout good"><span class="report-status">Baseline only</span><p>No Norway route has two different stored values yet. That means movement cannot be measured yet; it does not prove that every wait stayed flat before tracking began.</p></div>
  ) : (
    <><h2>Verified changes between stored UDI observations</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Previous</th><th>Later stored value</th><th>Direction</th></tr></thead><tbody>{changes.map(record => (<tr><td><a href={`/norway/${record.serviceSlug}/`}>{services.NO.get(record.serviceSlug).name}</a></td><td>{record.delta.prev_raw}</td><td>{record.value_raw}</td><td>{record.delta.dir === 'up' ? 'Longer' : 'Shorter'} {record.delta.pct}%</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div></>
  )}

  <h2>Last recorded planning spectrum</h2>
  <p>These bars put the normalized durations on one visual scale. They are a planning overview, not a performance ranking: the routes involve different decisions, authorities and starting points. Exact official wording remains beside every bar.</p>
  <div class="bar-list">
    {rows.map(record => (
      <div class="bar-row">
        <a href={`/norway/${record.serviceSlug}/`}>{services.NO.get(record.serviceSlug).name}</a>
        <div class="bar-track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar-fill" style={`width:${Math.max(3, record.value_days / maxDays * 100)}%`}></div></div>
        <span class="num">{record.value_raw}</span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Method and limits</h2>
  <p>The collector was limited to UDI’s complete server-rendered tables, required every mapped row and the official “Last updated” date, and failed the release if a table disappeared or an unknown row appeared. It is now removed from active collection because robots access returns HTTP 403; GovWait does not bypass that restriction. Personalised questionnaire pages remain outside this baseline. For the one stored visitor-visa range, the chart uses the upper end while the exact range remains visible.</p>
  <p>See <a href="/guides/how-norway-udi-waiting-times-work/">the Norway methodology guide</a> for clock boundaries, range handling and why personalised routes are excluded.</p>
  <div class="prov">Official sources: {sources.map((url, index) => <>{index ? ' · ' : ''}<a href={url} rel="noopener">UDI table {index + 1}</a></>)} · baseline source date {fmtDate(checked)} · last GovWait verification {fmtDate(source?.robots_checked_at)} · not immigration or legal advice.</div>
</EditorialFrame>
